Shared agent skills

codebase-design, diagnosing-bugs, grill-me, grilling, handoff, research, teach,
and wizard are adapted from Matt Pocock's skills,
https://github.com/mattpocock/skills, under the MIT license below. Local
adaptations name skills without harness-specific command syntax and keep each
skill's substantive workflow. Upstream changes up to commit 59db609
(2026-10-27) are merged.

- grill-me, grilling: skills/productivity, from 85f83d3. grilling asks
  settled-prerequisite questions in batches through the interactive question
  tool.
- handoff: skills/productivity, from d28dfdc.
- teach: skills/productivity, from 6654f6b. Agrees on a workspace before
  creating learning files inside a software project.
- codebase-design, diagnosing-bugs, research, wizard: skills/engineering,
  from 3cca18b. research uses available web tools without nested research
  agents; codebase-design and diagnosing-bugs cite current project
  documentation instead of a context summary; wizard's pause stops at EOF.

previews and yeet are this repository's own workflows.

babysit-pr, file-pr, full-send, full-stop, and sol-loop are copied unchanged
from Theo Browne's tstack, https://github.com/t3dotgg/tstack, at commit 1085050
(2026-10-27), under the MIT license below.

